{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779220114,"nonce":"RtdJOwWfPvqqJqzOg3NMOh2iBIg=","message":"## Cross-reference: task panel / scenario-boundary decision\n\nAdded the detailed task-as-scenario-boundary spec to `bda4721`.\n\nImpact on this issue: the value/timeline editor should be designed as part of the task/scenario panel, not as richer parameter editing on a graph task node. In particular:\n\n- delayed-task epochs, signal lanes, endpoint generation, catch trials, sampling scopes, and eval overrides should populate `StudioScenarioSpec.task_spec` plus a task-binding spec;\n- only explicitly bindable task outputs should appear as canvas-edge ports;\n- task-binding edges should not be normal component wires and should not imply full-state flow;\n- `inits`, targets, intervention schedules, and protocol values need separate roles instead of all being exposed as ordinary node output ports.\n\nPractical sequencing: do the task-boundary data model and minimal sidebar/left-edge binding surface before building the richer delayed-task value editor. That keeps the new editor from hardening the current fake task-node representation.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}